In a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/09/apple-smart-home-hub-september/">report on a planned September launch</a> for new &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; capabilities and the home hub that's reliant on the revamped version of &zwnj;Siri&zwnj;, Gurman says the updated &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; and &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; are both linked to "new artificial intelligence features."<br/>
<br/>
We've been hearing rumors about a new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod-mini/">HomePod mini</a> and a refreshed &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; 4K <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/12/12/apple-tv-homepod-mini-2025-launch/">since 2024</a>. Gurman said several times in 2025 that Apple was aiming for a launch before the end of the year, but <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/12/22/where-is-the-new-apple-tv/">no new Apple TV or HomePod materialized</a>. We also didn't hear a word about the devices at Apple's early 2026 launch event last week, which saw the introduction of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17e/">iPhone 17e</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-neo/">MacBook Neo</a>, and more.<br/>
<br/>
At this point, it seems like Apple may not introduce the new &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; 4K and &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; until the new version of &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; is ready. Apple was planning to debut the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> version of &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; in iOS 26.4, but the revamp has been pushed back because &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; still isn't working reliably. Apple is now aiming to launch all of the new &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; features in iOS 27 alongside the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18/">iPhone 18</a> Pro, though it's possible we could see some of the capabilities before September as part of an iOS 26.5 update.<br/>
<br/>
Gurman's wording today mentions a "&zwnj;HomePod&zwnj;" rather than a &zwnj;HomePod mini&zwnj; specifically, but in past reports, he has claimed that Apple has a new version of the &zwnj;HomePod mini&zwnj; ready to go. It's not clear if the larger &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; is also getting refreshed, or if Apple is only planning to update its smaller speaker.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; 4K hasn't been refreshed since 2022. Rumors suggest that it will get an A17 Pro chip and Apple's N1 networking chip, but no major design updates. The A17 Pro chip is capable of supporting &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; features, and it was previously used in the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/iphone/">iPhone</a> 15 Pro and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-mini/">iPad mini</a>.<br/>
